# Cloudflare Pages routing — mirrors app/vercel.json rewrites.
#
# /n8n/* is handled by the Pages Function at functions/n8n/[[path]].js (an
# external-origin proxy; _redirects cannot proxy external domains). Functions
# run BEFORE these rules, so /n8n/* never falls through to here.
#
# The app is built with Vite base '/poetech-app/', so index.html references its
# assets as /poetech-app/assets/... . The build output (dist) is published at
# the site ROOT, so map the /poetech-app/ prefix back to root — exactly the
# Vercel rewrite "/poetech-app/(.*) -> /$1". A 200 (rewrite, not redirect) keeps
# the URL bar on /poetech-app/ so the service-worker scope + Supabase auth
# redirect URLs (both pinned to /poetech-app/) stay correct.
# Her-name share links: /moore serves the static Moore Divahs entry page (its
# own og tags so a texted link previews as HER shop, then meta-refresh into the
# door). /mooredivahs is a spelled-out alias. public/moore/index.html is served
# automatically at /moore/; only the alias needs a rule.
/mooredivahs   /moore/  301
/mooredivahs/  /moore/  301

# The church's share links (DR-0133 phase install-identity): /lovecorner serves
# the static Church-of-the-Living-God entry page (its own og tags so a texted
# link previews as THE CHURCH, then meta-refresh into ?view=church).
# public/lovecorner/index.html is served automatically at /lovecorner/; only the
# aliases need rules. HELD Tier C — live only after Bishop Gwin + Governor.
/church        /lovecorner/  301
/church/       /lovecorner/  301
/thelovecorner   /lovecorner/  301
/thelovecorner/  /lovecorner/  301

# TLC Therapy Solutions' share links: /tlc serves the static TLC client-door
# entry page (its own og tags so a texted link previews as TLC, then meta-
# refresh into ?tlc=1). public/tlc/index.html is served automatically at /tlc/;
# only the spelled-out aliases need rules. HELD Tier C — live only after
# Christina Poe, LCSW reviews the content and greenlights the send.
/tlctherapy            /tlc/  301
/tlctherapy/           /tlc/  301
/tlctherapysolutions   /tlc/  301
/tlctherapysolutions/  /tlc/  301

# The bare root must land INSIDE the manifest scope (/poetech-app/), or the
# page a phone naturally opens (poetech.us) is out of scope and Chrome refuses
# to install the PWA entirely — no prompt, no "Install app" menu entry
# (2026-07-07, Darrell's phone). 302 on purpose: a 301 gets cached hard by
# browsers and would fight any future distinct root landing page. Query strings
# pass through, so shared ?join=1 / ?register links keep working.
/  /poetech-app/  302

/poetech-app/*  /:splat  200
